  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "With an array `points` where `points[i] = [xi, yi]` represents a point on the **X-Y** plane, output `true` *if these points are a **boomerang***.\n\nA **boomerang** is a set of three points that are **all distinct** and **not in a straight line**.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n```\nInput: points = [[1,1],[2,3],[3,2]]\nOutput: true\n```\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n```\nInput: points = [[1,1],[2,2],[3,3]]\nOutput: false\n```\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n* `points.length == 3`\n* `points[i].length == 2`\n* `0 <= xi, yi <= 100`",
    "constraints": [
      "None"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Single line: JSON array of all arguments, e.g. [arg1, arg2, ...]",
    "outputFormat": "Single line: JSON-serialised return value",
